{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey Security Deposit Law cap and return rules","requirement":"A landlord may not take a security deposit above 1.5 months' rent and may raise it by no more than 10% a year; the landlord must return the deposit with interest, less itemized deductions, within 30 days of the tenancy ending.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; annual deposit increase max 10%","coverage_conditions":"Applies to residential rentals in New Jersey; the deposit-holding and interest provisions do not apply to seasonal use or rental of 125 consecutive days or fewer.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"All residential rentals; seasonal use of 125 days or fewer exempt from holding and interest rules"},"exemptions":"Seasonal use or rental of not more than 125 consecutive days is exempt from the holding, interest and notice provisions; a landlord need not collect a deposit at all.","penalty":"Tenant may sue for double the amount of the deposit wrongfully withheld, plus court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19 et seq.","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Safe Housing Act deposit return after domestic violence lease termination","requirement":"When a tenant ends a lease early under the Safe Housing Act, the landlord must make the security deposit plus earned interest available within 15 business days and give written notice of when and where to collect it within three business days.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who terminate a lease because they or their child face an imminent threat of serious physical harm; transient or seasonal rentals are excluded.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Tenancies ended early by a domestic violence victim under the Safe Housing Act"},"exemptions":"Transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
